BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Melissa  King: The Girl Who Became King
DTSTART:20261106T020000Z
DTEND:20261106T040000Z
DTSTAMP:20261101T124323Z
UID:0743b5f8-c6a1-59a1-834d-61b5c20d04a5
DESCRIPTION:From James Beard award-winning chef\, author and television pe
 rsonality Melissa King comes an intimate\, captivating memoir about family
 \, food and finding her voice as a queer Chinese American chef: “Embraci
 ng my love of food has empowered me to embrace every layer of who I am: my
  Chinese heritage\, my American upbringing\, and all the parts of me that 
 felt too much and not enough. When I chose myself\, I set her free. Just m
 e. The girl who became king.”\n\nMore info & tickets: https://www.common
 wealthclub.org/events/2026-11-05/melissa-king-girl-who-became-king
LOCATION:Commonwealth Club World Affairs of California\, Taube Family Audi
 torium\, San Francisco\, CA
URL:https://www.commonwealthclub.org/events/2026-11-05/melissa-king-girl-w
 ho-became-king
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Imperfect Circles Discussion Group at the Orinda Library
DTSTART:20261106T023000Z
DTEND:20261106T043000Z
DTSTAMP:20261101T124323Z
UID:ee054dbe-641a-518a-b8ab-0f0fd3d3161b
DESCRIPTION:Are you a person who never tires of talking or thinking about 
 philosophical\, scientific or religious theories? Are you interested in ps
 ychological insights\, or attempts at such insights\, into human life? The
 re are many who would insist that being realistic about human life means y
 ou should ignore such fundamental questions—starting around the time the
  ink dries on your diploma. But it is unrealistic to ignore the fundamenta
 l explanatory concepts that underlie each successful human civilization—
 concepts that sometimes help and sometimes hinder us in our pursuit of hap
 piness.\n\nMore info & tickets: https://www.commonwealthclub.org/events/20
 26-11-05/imperfect-circles-discussion-group-orinda-library
LOCATION:Orinda Public Library\, 26 Orinda Way\, Orinda\, CA
URL:https://www.commonwealthclub.org/events/2026-11-05/imperfect-circles-d
 iscussion-group-orinda-library
END:VEVENT
