BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:UC Berkeley’s Saira Mohamed on “What a Country Owes Its Soldie
 rs”
DTSTART:20261117T013000Z
DTEND:20261117T033000Z
DTSTAMP:20261101T124323Z
UID:33291184-74d0-5f71-bb53-4d937d63646b
DESCRIPTION:American leaders endlessly profess their admiration for milita
 ry service members. But according to UC Berkeley law professor Saira Moham
 ed\, these effusive declarations hardly comport with reality. Soldiers rec
 eive shoddy equipment and inadequate medical care\; they are ordered to co
 mmit crimes and deployed to illegal wars. Such treatment\, she writes\, is
  rarely recognized for what it is: a violation of the duty owed to soldier
 s by their government.\n\nMore info & tickets: https://www.commonwealthclu
 b.org/events/2026-11-16/uc-berkeleys-saira-mohamed-what-country-owes-its-s
 oldiers
LOCATION:Commonwealth Club World Affairs of California\, Third Floor\, San
  Francisco\, CA
URL:https://www.commonwealthclub.org/events/2026-11-16/uc-berkeleys-saira-
 mohamed-what-country-owes-its-soldiers
END:VEVENT
