DESCRIPTION:David Y. Lei\, born in Taiwan\, immigrated to the United State
 s in 1956. He began his career as a social worker in San Francisco’s Chi
 natown in the late 1960s\, working with young people involved in Chinatown
  gangs. In 1981\, he entered the business world\, exporting consumer produ
 cts to Mexico. He sold his business in 2003 and retired. Lei served as vic
 e chair of the Asian Art Museum board and directed San Francisco’s Chine
 se New Year Parade from 1977 to 2006.\n\nMore info & tickets: https://www.
 commonwealthclub.org/events/2027-01-14/chinese-americans-most-litigious-ci
