DESCRIPTION:What drove a few thousand men and women from the deserts and c
 ities of western China to the front lines of Syria’s war? In her new boo
 k\, Our Hearts Burned for Home\, journalist Emily Feng unearths the untold
  story of Uyghur exiles who fled China’s expanding police state—only t
 o become a pivotal force behind the fall of Bashar al-Assad’s regime. At
  the heart of this narrative is a startling paradox: Beijing’s repressio
 n\, meant to crush dissent\, instead scattered and radicalized a generatio
 n. \n\nMore info & tickets: https://www.commonwealthclub.org/events/2027-
